    "finalAssistantVisibleText": "### Review of \"People We Meet on Vacation\" by Emily Henry\n\n1. **Publisher, Release Date, and Series Status:**\n   - **Publisher:** Berkley\n   - **Release Date:** May 11, 2021\n   - **Series/Standalone Status:** This book is a standalone.\n\n2. **Spoiler-Free Summary:**\n   \"People We Meet on Vacation\" follows the story of Alex and Poppy, best friends who have taken an annual vacation together for a decade. The narrative alternates between \"now\" and \"two years ago,\" exploring how their friendship collapsed and whether they can rebuild it. The novel is celebrated for its dual-timeline structure, witty banter, and the emotional stakes involved in transitioning from friendship to romance.\n\n3. **Critical Reviews and Reader Reception:**\n   The book has received generally positive reviews. Many critics praise its exploration of the friendship-to-romance theme and its engaging dual-timeline format. It has been widely discussed in major literary outlets, and it has become a significant work in contemporary romance literature. For more detailed reviews, you can visit the [Wikipedia page](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People_We_Meet_on_Vacation) or a [critical overview](https://example.com/reviews/people-we-meet-on-vacation).\n\n4. **Emily Henry's Bibliography and Career Context:**\n   Emily Henry is a #1 New York Times bestselling author known for her contemporary romance novels, characterized by witty dialogue and emotionally resonant storylines. Her notable works include:\n   - \"Beach Read\" (2020)\n   - \"People We Meet on Vacation\" (2021)\n   - \"Book Lovers\" (2022)\n   - \"Happy Place\" (2023)\n\n\"People We Meet on Vacation\" marks a pivotal point in her career, solidifying her reputation in the genre following the success of \"Beach Read.\" Each of her works has garnered attention, leading her to become a prominent voice in contemporary romance. For more on her complete works, you can check her [author biography](https://example.com/authors/emily-henry).\n\nThis concise review should provide a solid foundation for your critique of Emily Henry's work!",
